hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"114","Yanfuthu 'an yasārihi (thalāthan). Yasta'īdhu billāhi min ash-shaitāni wa min sharri mā ra'ā (thalātha marrāt). Lā yuhaddithu bihā ahadan. Yatahawwala 'an janbi-hi alladhī kāna 'alayhi.. He blows to his left side (three times). He seeks refuge in Allah from Satan and from the evil of what he has seen (three times). He does not tell anyone about it. He turns over to the other side of what he was lying on."
"115","Yaqūmu yuṣallī in arāda dhālika.. He stands to pray if he wishes to do so."
